  "name": "Company Brain - Cognee RAG Agent (Full, Annotated)",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "d5dfa4d6-bf1f-43d1-9356-d66cfe7cdd91",
      "name": "📌 Overview – How This Workflow Works",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -2144,
        -720
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 844,
        "height": 720,
        "content": "## 🧠 Company Brain – Cognee RAG Knowledge Agent\n\n### How it works\nThis workflow builds a company knowledge base using Cognee's graph-based RAG and exposes it as a conversational AI agent. **Ingestion:** a manual trigger downloads a PDF from Google Drive, extracts the text, and adds it to Cognee's `company_brain` dataset — building the knowledge graph. **Query:** when someone asks a question via the n8n chat UI or a Slack message, the Company Brain Agent uses GPT-4o-mini with a Cognee search tool to return a contextually grounded answer. Slack questions get posted back to the channel; web chat questions are returned via a Set node so the chat UI displays the response. A global error trigger catches any failure and posts a structured alert to your Slack ops channel.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Connect **Cognee API** to both Cognee nodes (`Add Data to Cognee` and `Search in cognee memory in Cognee`).\n2. Connect **Google Drive OAuth2** and set `YOUR_DRIVE_FILE_ID` to your first document for ingestion.\n3. Connect **OpenAI API** to the OpenAI Chat Model node.\n4. Connect **Slack API** to the Slack Trigger and Reply in Slack nodes — set `YOUR_SLACK_CHANNEL_ID`.\n5. Connect **Slack OAuth2** to the Notify Error in Slack node — set `YOUR_SLACK_ERROR_CHANNEL_ID`.\n6. Run `When clicking 'Add to Brain'` manually to ingest your first document.\n7. Activate both the Chat trigger and the Slack trigger."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "198da9c4-19f0-4064-934d-cfee626bad7e",
      "name": "Section – Document Ingestion Pipeline",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1152,
        -720
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1200,
        "height": 536,
        "content": "## 📄 Document Ingestion Pipeline\nManually triggered. Downloads a PDF from Google Drive, extracts the raw text, and adds it to Cognee's `company_brain` dataset. Run this each time you want to add a new document to the knowledge graph. Extend by looping over a Drive folder for bulk ingestion."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "9f922a00-a436-4cac-bdab-ab437c396ed4",
      "name": "Section – Dual-Trigger Query Agent",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1136,
        -144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 988,
        "height": 872,
        "content": "## 💬 Dual-Trigger Query Agent\nAccepts questions from the n8n built-in chat UI or a Slack message. Both paths feed the Company Brain Agent, which searches Cognee's knowledge graph, reasons with GPT-4o-mini and conversation memory, and returns a grounded answer."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "7854b8ac-7fb8-417b-91e7-2b37f854c4c8",
      "name": "Section – Response Routing",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -96,
        -128
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 796,
        "height": 648,
        "content": "## 📣 Response Routing\nAfter the agent responds, a check determines where the question came from. Slack questions get a reply posted back to the channel. Web chat questions flow to **Set Chat Response**, which sets the `output` field — n8n's chat trigger reads this automatically and displays it in the chat window."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e24dddff-c258-4df2-91e0-efa9018fbef3",
      "name": "Section – Error Handling",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        80,
        672
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 964,
        "height": 456,
        "content": "## ⚠️ Error Handling\nA workflow-level error trigger catches any node failure. The error details are structured into a Slack alert — workflow name, failed node, error message, and timestamp — and posted to your ops channel."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "3b8f6027-eb41-43e8-88d6-4fd591360491",
      "name": "🔑 Credentials & Configuration",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        832,
        160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 400,
        "height": 360,
        "content": "## 🔑 Credentials Required\n- **Cognee API** — ingestion + search (both Cognee nodes)\n- **Google Drive OAuth2** — document download\n- **OpenAI API** — GPT-4o-mini LLM\n- **Slack API** — trigger + reply in channel\n- **Slack OAuth2** — error alerts channel\n\nNever hardcode API keys or channel IDs in shared templates."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
